Pages of the contestant site of the original CMS (Contest Management System,
https://github.com/cms-dev/cms, AGPL-3.0-or-later; copyright © the CMS
contributors), version 1.6.dev0 (commit 1914a5a), as it served them for the
demo contest of testdata/dumps/demo (the dump was exported from that same
installation), captured with Python's urllib on 2026-10-15:

  contest_list.html    GET /
  login.html           GET /demo                      (not logged in)
  login_error.html     GET /demo?login_error=true&next=%2Fdemo%2Fdocumentation
  error_404.html       GET /nosuch                    (unknown contest)
  overview.html        GET /demo                      (logged in as alice)
  documentation.html   GET /demo/documentation        (logged in as alice;
                       contest_web_server.docs_path set to a directory
                       without language documentation)
  register.html        GET /demo/register             (allow_registration and
  login_register.html  GET /demo                       two teams, ita and arg)
  communication*.html  GET /demo/communication        (logged in as alice):
                       communication.html with the announcements, messages
                       and questions of insertCommunication
                       (communication_test.go), _empty without them,
                       _noquestions with allow_questions false, _before
                       before the start of the contest

TestCMSPages (pages_test.go; TestCMSCommunication in communication_test.go
for communication*.html) renders the same pages and compares them byte
for byte after replacing what changes between requests (static file hashes,
CSRF tokens, times) and the documented differences of this fork (D10: CSP
nonce, handlers moved out of the HTML, comments html/template drops; R5.8:
live updates indicator; N8: link to the source code; R2.2: the
explanation of the outcome of the seccomp filter in the documentation;
R5.5 and R5.9 on the communication page: the attributes of the live
regions, their script, and contest times whose title is the time CMS
shows).

token_rules.json holds what format_token_rules of CMS (formatting.py)
returns for the token rules of TestFormatTokenRules (pages_test.go) in
seven languages, recorded by calling it with CMS's own translations.

tasks/ holds what the same CMS answered on the task pages: descriptions,
statements and attachments, the submissions of a task in every status
(official or not, with and without tokens, limits, analysis mode, after
the end), the status JSON, the details of each score type, the file
downloads (headers), the testing page, its JSON, details and downloads,
in a few languages. scenarios.json lists the states (SQL on the demo
contest, for user carol) and the requests; capture.py applied them to a
copy of the reference database and recorded the answers in
captured.json.gz. TestCMSTaskPages (tasks_cms_test.go) applies the same
SQL to the demo dump, sets the clock to the time of each capture and
compares status, Location, Content-Type, Content-Disposition, the JSON
values and the pages (normalized as above, plus: the attributes of the
live regions, the contest times of the rows whose title is the time CMS
shows, the onchange handlers of the file inputs and the comments of the
scripts). Two answers differ on purpose and are checked for what this
fork shows: the public details of a subtask with private testcases (CMS
fails and says "Score details temporarily unavailable."; R5.4) and the
times of the submission rows in Japanese (CMS formats them in English).
